{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>She shall not go out as the going out of the slaves</b> — as the going out of Canaanite slaves with tooth and eye. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 21:7). And so our Sages expounded it (Mekhilta here). And this is correct, for a Hebrew slave is not called a \"slave\" in the unqualified term. And I wonder: why did the verse need to say this? Perhaps it is so that we not reason concerning the Hebrew woman that she should also go out with tooth and eye by an a fortiori inference from the Canaanite woman. It stated this concerning the Hebrew woman and equated the Hebrew man to her. But the author of the Halakhot Gedolot wrote: since the going out of slaves with tooth and eye is a penalty, and we do not learn from penalties, Scripture made this a negative commandment, warning the master that if he comes to remove her from his domain with tooth and eye he transgresses a negative prohibition, but he must pay the value of the tooth and the eye, and she shall remain with him for designation until the time, for this would be a great wrong — that he knocked out her tooth in his anger with her and then removes her from the house to which she had been looking forward to his designation, after he had blemished her. Moreover, the value of the damage to the principal limbs may often exceed the value of her service when the time is near at hand. And Scripture was stringent upon the master with a negative prohibition, that he not rob her of the value of her principal limbs even if he wishes to release her with them. And it is possible that the release itself is forbidden to him until the time, for Scripture obligated him in her food, and to remain with him — perhaps she will find favor in his eyes and be designated — just as it warned with a negative prohibition concerning her food, her clothing, and her conjugal rights, that he not diminish. And according to this opinion, <b>she shall not go out as the going out of the slaves</b> is counted among the 365 negative commandments."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:12:58.297220507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}